{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For</b> — He mentioned arms, for they draw bows. And he mentioned that the bows will be broken, so no harm comes to the righteous. And he mentioned that the arms likewise. And the opposite of 'will be broken' he juxtaposes [i.e., 'will be sustained']."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:56.540481407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}